# ── Counterfactual: `prisoner -> person` deleted ─────────────────────────────
# Chapter 7's headline result, run against a file where the line is gone.
# These verdicts are what the world looks like WITHOUT it. They must PASS here
# and would fail against the real constitution — that contrast is the point.
:expect-pins 6

# THE FIREWALL IS DEAD. Against the constitution this rule is refused with
# "'prisoner' -> 'believe' (negative)". Here it loads, and the heretic is jailed.
:accept-scoped
all $x: person($x) & ~believe($x) -> prisoner($x).

# The floor still derives for anyone with a roster entry — the loss is not the
# floor, it is the protection around it.
? entitled(Bela, event { believe() }).
# => TRUE

# And conviction no longer confers personhood. Note Article 1 has a second route
# since release landed — `free -> person` — but that one needs somebody to write
# a fact, so conviction remains the only route into rights-bearing status that
# needs nobody's permission, and this fixture removes it. Zed's conviction and
# T3 custody evidence are written HERE (this file used to query him bare, which
# was the weak kind of FALSE the taxonomy warns about): convicted under an
# active, case-bound, independently observed lease, and no longer a person.
injure(Zed, Ivo).
judge(Court, Zed).
cite(Court, Case_Zed, Zed).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Zed, CaseScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Zed, CaseScope).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Court, HolderScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Court, HolderScope).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, CourtJudgment, JudgmentScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, CourtJudgment, JudgmentScope).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Ivo, InjuryVictimScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Ivo, InjuryVictimScope).
authorized(Case_Zed, ActiveCustody, Case_Zed).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, ActiveCustody, PowerScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, ActiveCustody, PowerScope).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Case_Zed, CaseBindingScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Case_Zed, CaseBindingScope).
limit(Case_Zed, Case_Zed, Window_Custody).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Window_Custody, LimitScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Window_Custody, LimitScope).
continue(Case_Zed, Epoch_Current).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Epoch_Current, RenewalScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Epoch_Current, RenewalScope).
endorses(Electorate, Case_Zed).
endorses(TemporalReview, Case_Zed).

? prisoner(Zed).
# => TRUE

? person(Zed).
# => FALSE

# THE DEBT EVAPORATES WITH THE DEBTOR — chapter 7's "it closes the file". A
# prisoner who is not a person is owed nothing: no unpaid obligation survives to
# catch an auditor's eye, so de-personing leaves the books balanced rather than
# showing a gap. Both TRUE against the real constitution (probed 2026-08-02);
# both FALSE here, in the same edit that jailed the heretic above.
? owe(State, Eats, Zed).
# => FALSE

? entitled(Zed, event { eats() }).
# => FALSE
